 `applyPatch(document, patch)` applies an RFC 6902 JSON Patch array and returns a new value. It supports
 `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`; malformed operations, unresolved paths, and
-failed tests throw an error. The input document is left unchanged.
+failed tests throw an error and stop processing the patch. Operations are applied in order, and the
+input document is left unchanged even when an operation fails.
 
 ```ts
 import { applyPatch } from "json-toolkit";
